{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr42ami4z24","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"ARC EWM harness design spec five pillars","summary":"Approved design for the new ARC-AGI-3 harness (feature arc-ewm-harness), built in bench/arc_agi3_zonoid/ewm/, Mode B (official checkout patch) as reference integration. Pillar 1 VISION: two LLM calls per decision turn — call A (decide) gets ONE composite PNG (last frame | current frame | diff-mask panel, labels baked in, 4x nearest-neighbor upscale, 16-color ARC palette); call B (reflect) gets current|result composite + structured action result; images never retained in history. Pillar 2 REPL: sandboxed Python subprocess, preloaded current_frame/previous_frame/history/transitions/valid_actions/action()/remaining_actions/remaining_seconds; whitelisted stdlib imports; 30s per execution; segmentation helper (4-connected components, Moore contour corners, translation-invariant SHA1 object hashes) ported from duck-harness. Pillar 3 BUDGET GUARDS: action() refuses batches beyond remaining budget; mid-batch abort on k consecutive no-ops, level transition, score regression, or per-action predicted-frame mismatch; returns {executed_count, stop_reason}. Pillar 4 EXECUTABLE WORLD MODEL: LLM synthesizes step(state,action)->(state,events) grid-in/grid-out Python program with declared-UNKNOWN partial fidelity; every observed real transition becomes a regression test the program must replay; repair by minimal patch on first failing transition; planning is CPU search (BFS/rollouts) against step(), zero LLM tokens; loop = SYNTHESIZE->VALIDATE->PLAN->EXECUTE->DIVERGE->REPAIR. Pillar 5 KB ROLE: program+test suite are within-game memory; KB is version store + transfer layer — ORIENT does keyed lookup \"game <id> world model program\"; SYNTHESIZE searches cross-game mechanic patterns by segmentation vocabulary; REPAIR searches failed-repair notes + mechanic patterns; PLAN/EXECUTE never touch KB; writes only at acceptance events (program revision supersedes prior, level solution, confirmed cross-game mechanic pattern, modelability verdict, failed-repair note); harness caps 1-2 notes/turn; ","category":null,"tags":["arc-agi-3","ewm","design-spec","duck-harness"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-02T22:14:12.844Z","vec":[-0.03150038421154022,-0.025225380435585976,-0.0447903610765934,-0.005069841630756855,0.07299865782260895,-0.04320128634572029,-0.025809498503804207,0.052957866340875626,-0.014601616188883781,0.03964291885495186,0.008954334072768688,-0.0523776076734066,0.0356208011507988,-0.03854912146925926,-0.00612519821152091,0.022451573982834816,0.034971725195646286,0.011467707343399525,-0.10957124084234238,-0.06232747435569763,0.07902839034795761,-0.05766851082444191,0.02307845465838909,-0.0032188561744987965,-0.05525514855980873,0.0015697191702201962,-0.050254303961992264,-0.017450295388698578,-0.04667261242866516,-0.1303270012140274,0.0009918782161548734,0.10328032076358795,0.03821764513850212,0.018198905512690544,-0.019633106887340546,0.06257405132055283,-0.008932942524552345,-0.0628616064786911,-0.10227761417627335,-0.09459157288074493,-0.025793004781007767,0.010146587155759335,-0.022601841017603874,-0.04094361513853073,0.044693347066640854,-0.015270943753421307,-0.0778927356004715,-0.10499395430088043,-0.06771335005760193,0.009315944276750088,-0.05128234624862671,-0.024843906983733177,-0.04297667369246483,0.05087212100625038,0.06092959642410278,0.0737452581524849,0.07227608561515808,0.0115412762388587,-0.017650771886110306,-0.027696829289197922,0.0216731745749712,-0.0750882551074028,-0.06561540812253952,-0.001976612489670515,-0.004413697402924299,0.009405802935361862,0.0713968425989151,-0.06210145354270935,0.05709570646286011,-0.032951321452856064,-0.07345212996006012,-0.027708206325769424,-0.03395318239927292,-0.01537603884935379,-0.0023254933767020702,0.08516952395439148,0.09734167158603668,0.027167757973074913,0.011879026889801025,-0.14155463874340057,-0.0348367914557457,0.08241311460